    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n,s;\\n\\tif (scanf(\\\"%d %d\\\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\\n\\tstd::vector<int> matrix(n*n);\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &matrix[i*n+j]);\\n\\n\\tassert(s<n && n<8000 && s>0 && n>0);\\n\\n\\tstd::vector<long long> colSum(n, 0);\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++) {\\n\\t\\tconst int* row = &matrix[i*n];\\n\\t\\t#pragma omp simd\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++)\\n\\t\\t\\tcolSum[j] += (long long)row[j];\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tstd::vector<long long> pref(n+1);\\n\\tlong long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\\n\\n\\tfor(int i=0; i+s<=n; ++i) {\\n\\t\\tpref[0]=0;\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++)\\n\\t\\t\\tpref[j+1] = pref[j] + colSum[j];\\n\\n\\t\\tlong long rowMax = LLONG_MIN;\\n\\t\\t#pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowMax)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0; j+s<=n; ++j) {\\n\\t\\t\\tlong long val = pref[j+s]-pref[j];\\n\\t\\t\\tif(val > rowMax) rowMax = val;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif(rowMax > mxSum) mxSum = rowMax;\\n\\n\\t\\tif(i+s < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\tconst int* addRow = &matrix[(i+s)*n];\\n\\t\\t\\tconst int* subRow = &matrix[i*n];\\n\\t\\t\\t#pragma omp simd\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcolSum[j] += (long long)addRow[j] - (long long)subRow[j];\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%lld\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Replacing the O(SN^2) snake sliding-window traversal with an O(N^2) column-sum + prefix algorithm reduces arithmetic complexity. The independent column-update and max-reduction loops are explicitly SIMD-vectorized, while the only sequential dependency (the per-row prefix scan) remains short. Using 64-bit accumulators for intermediate column sums preserves correctness even when individual columns exceed int32 range.\",\n  \"notes\": \"The algorithm maintains a running sum of each column