        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i*n+j]);\n\n    assert(s<n && n<8000 && s>0 && n>0);\n\n    std::vector<long long> colSum(n, 0);\n    // initial column sums: first s rows\n    for(int i=0;i<s;i++) {\n        const int* row = &matrix[i*n];\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++)\n            colSum[j] += (long long)row[j];\n    }\n\n    std::vector<long long> pref(n+1);\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN; // or use -9e18\n\n    for(int i=0; i+s<=n; ++i) {\n        // prefix sums\n        pref[0]=0;\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++)\n            pref[j+1] = pref[j] + colSum[j];\n\n        long long rowMax = LLONG_MIN;\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowMax)\n        for(int j=0; j+s<=n; ++j) {\n            long long val = pref[j+s]-pref[j];\n            if(val > rowMax) rowMax = val;\n        }\n        if(rowMax > mxSum) mxSum = rowMax;\n\n        // update colSum for next top row\n        if(i+s < n) {\n            const int* addRow = &matrix[(i+s)*n];\n            const int* subRow = &matrix[i*n];\n            #pragma omp simd\n            for(int j=0;j<n;j++)\n                colSum[j] += (long long)addRow[j] - (long long)subRow[j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n}\n\nBut note: The output must be int32, but printing as %lld is fine if value fits. However the reference expects decimal integer; using %lld prints correctly.\n\nPotential issue: The prefix loop has a dependency and may not vectorize, but it's O(n) per row. Could we avoid prefix by maintaining horizontal running sum? That would have sequential add/sub dependencies too. Prefix allows SIMD max reduction. Let's keep.\n\nWe can also try to combine the update with next iteration's prefix? Not needed.\n\nAnother optimization: Instead of recomputing prefix from scratch each i, we could maintain a sliding window horizontally as in baseline but using colSum; that would be O(n) per row with sequential dependency chain length n-s. The prefix